        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: കുഴി",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കുഴി — kuḻi — \"a pothole; a pit\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വഴിയിലെ വലിയ കുഴിയിൽ ബൈക്ക് വീണു. vaḻiyile valiya kuḻiyil baikkŭ vīṇu. The motorbike fell into a big pothole in the road."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: കുഴികൾ, kuḻikaḷ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Any hole in the ground: a pit, a grave, a pothole."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കുഴി (kuḻi) is native Dravidian, \"a hollow, a hole, a pit\" (DEDR 1818)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
